# Web: Outbound links (`rel` / SEO)

Default posture for third-party `<a target="_blank">` is **nofollow**. Pass link equity only for allowlisted brand / first-party destinations. Shared policy lives in `$lib/utils/externalLinkRel`.

## Policy (Option A)

| Destination | `trusted` | `follow` | Typical `rel` |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Configured brand social (`SOCIAL_LINKS_*` via `getSocialProfileHref`) | yes | yes | _(omit)_ |
| First-party GitHub (`FIRST_PARTY_GITHUB_OWNERS`, e.g. `Ratimon/…`) | yes | yes | _(omit)_ |
| `*.openquok.com`, `npmjs.com` | yes | yes | _(omit)_ |
| Self-host → hosted marketing (`hostedMarketingAnchorAttrs`) | n/a | n/a | `noopener` only — see **web-hosted-marketing-links** |
| All other absolute http(s) | no | no | `noopener noreferrer nofollow` |

Do **not** treat all of `github.com` as followable. Hub listing setup / source-repo buttons must call `resolveExternalLinkPolicy` / `externalLinkRelForHref` (or `ExternalLink` with those flags) — never hardcode `trusted` + `follow` on arbitrary third-party URLs.

## Helpers

- `resolveExternalLinkPolicy(href)` → `{ trusted, follow }`
- `externalLinkRelForHref(href)` → `rel` string (or `undefined` when followable)
- `externalLinkAnchorAttrs(href)` → `{ href, target: '_blank', rel, trusted, follow }`
- `isConfiguredBrandSocialHref` / `isFirstPartyGithubHref` / `isTrustedExternalHref`

Prefer these over hand-rolled `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.

## Components

- **`ExternalLink`**: low-level; defaults are untrusted + nofollow. Pass `trusted` / `follow` from the policy when the destination is allowlisted.
- **`DocsExternalLink` / `DocsLinkCard`**: auto-apply `resolveExternalLinkPolicy` unless props override.
- **Brand social UI** (`SocialFollowBar`, `DiscordSupportFab`, footer Discord via `InternalLinkBar`, `DocsSocialLinks`): must end up followable for configured profile URLs.
- **`Stargazers` / listing source repos / setup-doc buttons**: policy-driven (first-party GitHub / openquok.com follow; third-party nofollow).

## Do not confuse with hosted marketing

Relative marketing paths rewritten to `https://www.openquok.com/...` on self-host use **`hostedMarketingHref`**, not `ExternalLink` defaults. That path stays dofollow with `rel="noopener"` only — documented in **web-hosted-marketing-links**.

## Checklist

1. New outbound `<a>` / `Button` / `ExternalLink` → decide allowlist vs third-party.
2. Allowlisted → `trusted` + `follow` (or `externalLinkAnchorAttrs`).
3. Third-party → leave ExternalLink defaults (or `externalLinkRelForHref`).
4. Brand social URLs come from `getSocialProfileHref`, not hard-coded invites (except tests).
5. Extend `FIRST_PARTY_GITHUB_OWNERS` only when adding another first-party GitHub owner.
